> Customizing Mango - Autostart

Autostart configuration is in ~/.config/mango/autostart.conf

### exec-once vs exec

`exec-once`: runs once when mango starts (not on config reload).
`exec`: runs every time the config is reloaded (*super+R*).

### SNAPS-OS Pre-configured Autostart

exec-once entries (in order):

1. xdg-desktop-portal: portal service for file dialogs and screen sharing.
2. tldr --update: updates the TLDR command database.
3. dsearch serve: file indexer for DMS search, indexes ~ recursively (excludes hidden).
4. hyprpolkitagent: polkit authentication agent.
5. ~/.config/snapsos/firstrun.sh: first-run setup UI.
6. nautilus --gapplication-service: file manager background service.
7. dcal run -d --hidden: Dank Calendar daemon in background.
8. ~/.config/snapsos/wayshell/wayshell.sh: wayshell daemon for screenshot/OSD.
9. opentabletdriver: tablet driver service.
10. dms run: launches Dank Material Shell.
11. ghostty: pre-opens a terminal window.
12-14. toggle_named_scratchpad x3: pre-loads the terminal scratchpad on primary display
    (staggered at 2.5s, 3s, 3.5s delays).

### Adding Your Own

add apps you want on startup:
exec-once=path/to/your/app
exec-once=firefox (example)

for commands that should run on every reload:
exec=notify-send "config reloaded"

note: all paths use ~/.config/snapsos/... for SNAPS-OS scripts.
